<title>USA: TABLE - Regent Bancshares Q2 net loss narrows.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Regent Bancshares Q2 net loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>PHILADELPHIA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months   Six Months</p>
<p>					 Ended June 30,  Ended June 30,</p>
<p>				     1997     1996	1997     1996</p>
<p> Net Interest Income	  1,447    2,476     3,037    4,532</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses    300    3,875	 100    4,050</p>
<p>  Gains on sale of assets	23	 83	 568	 83</p>
<p> Income tax benefit	   (900)    (145)     (900)	---</p>
<p>INCOME (LOSS) before</p>
<p>preferred stock dividend</p>
<p>  and minority interest	  31  (2,970)     (149)  (2,752)</p>
<p>Loss before minority</p>
<p>  interest			 (96)  (2,901)     (360)  (2,828)</p>
<p> Net loss			 (129)  (2,901)     (393)  (2,828)</p>
<p> Earnings per share	  (0.04)   (2.61)    (0.18)   (2.56)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Regent Bancshares Corp said it paid preferred dividends of 10 percent of its stock value once a year.</p>
<p>Preferred dividends of $127,800 were accounted for in the second quarter of 1997, as compared to $68,900 in the second quarter of 1996.  Preferred dividends of $210,900 were accounted for in the first six months of 1997, as compared to a loss of $75,700 in the first six months of 1996.</p>
<p>Net income was calculated before the payment of preferred dividends, earnings per share were calculated after the payment of preferred dividends.</p>
